;;; conjurer.cnj
;;; The charter of the Conjurer language itself.
;;;
;;; The specification argues that intent is the source and every artefact a
;;; build of it. This file applies that to the specification: the reasons for
;;; the language's shape live here, not only in the CHANGELOG, the proposals
;;; and the conversations in which they were decided.
;;;
;;; Decisions taken before 2026-10-13 were recovered, not authored here. Each
;;; carries :recovered with its grade and :source with the record it was read
;;; from, as x/charter would emit them. Where the why was never written down,
;;; it is an :open question rather than a reason supplied after the fact.

;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;; Section 1 — Charter
;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(charter "Conjurer"
  :version  "0.1.0"
  :created  "2026-10-13"
  :updated  "2026-10-13"
  :domain   "Conjurer, a declarative language for working with LLMs: its
             philosophy (conjurer.md), the twelve standard grimoires, the
             template for grimoires and .cnj files, the symbol catalogue
             (index.edn), the entry documents for processors and readers, and
             the worked examples."
  :language :en

  :goals [
    "Keep intent as the source: a .cnj file is the durable statement of what
     should exist, and code is a build that can be regenerated, retargeted or
     discarded."
    "Say honestly what is deterministic and what is semantic: every binding
     statement can be traced to the layer that holds it, and nothing claims a
     layer it cannot reach."
    "Make uncertainty part of the language: how well something is known is
     graded, and a guess is never presented as a fact."
    "Run the flow both ways: intent manifests forward into artefacts, and
     artefacts are exhumed back into intent."
    "Stay small and coherent: grow the language from real use, keep its form
     symmetric, and prefer the elegant solution to the complete one."]

  :audience {:primary   :maintainer
             :secondary [:practitioner :llm-processor :tool-builder]}

  :decisions [

    ;; ── Recovered: repository and baseline ─────────────────────────

    {:id        :clean-grimoire-names
     :date      "2026-05-22"
     :decision  "Grimoire files carry clean names without numeric prefixes
                 (core.md, not 010_core_cnj.md)."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "git: the first scaffolding commit already uses clean names;
                 the maintainer's design notes state the rule as never to be
                 broken"
     :note      "Why was not recorded here; the maintainer gave his reason on
                 2026-10-13 (:decision/no-numeric-prefixes-why)."}

    {:id        :determinism-boundary
     :date      "2026-06-05"
     :decision  "Tooling for Conjurer embeds no model. Parsing, validation,
                 references and dependency order are deterministic and belong to
                 a processor such as conjurer-mcp; interpreting meaning belongs to
                 the model in the editor. Reason recorded at the time: a small,
                 testable, fast server without keys or model dependencies."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "examples/conjurer-mcp/conjurer-mcp.cnj, decision of 2026-06-05;
                 architecture.md, The determinism boundary"}

    {:id        :exhume-as-inverse
     :date      "2026-06-06"
     :decision  "The standard library includes exhume, the reverse flow: code is
                 read back into specification, every claim graded attested or
                 inferred."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md 1.0.0"}

    {:id        :changelog-baseline
     :date      "2026-06-06"
     :decision  "The changelog starts at the maturity baseline of 1.0.0; earlier
                 exploratory evolution is pre-history."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md, preamble"}

    {:id        :foresight-grimoire
     :date      "2026-06-10"
     :decision  "Deferred ideas are first-class: foresight records graded
                 candidates, appends reassessments to their :history, and closes
                 them with f/hoist. Abandonment is a status, not an event, so
                 there is no f/abandon."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md 1.1.0; foresight.md, Hoist as an event, abandon as
                 a status"}

    {:id        :materialise-two-phase
     :date      "2026-06-10"
     :decision  "materialise runs a deterministic preflight before semantic
                 generation and halts on unresolved references by default:
                 verify the lossless plan before risking the lossy act."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md 1.1.0; conjurer.md, Symmetry compresses; broken
                 symmetry informs"}

    ;; ── Recovered: the July evaluation ──────────────────────────────

    {:id        :abstraction-layer
     :date      "2026-07-01"
     :decision  "Practitioners name their own patterns: spell, charm and
                 incantation in core, and grimoire for packaging them. :forbids
                 joins the intent topology on conjure, with the force of
                 :requires and the opposite sign."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-07-spec-evaluation.md, Part V"}

    {:id        :verification-stays-layered
     :date      "2026-07-01"
     :decision  "No unified verification grimoire. Verification stays spread
                 over ensure, data/generate-tests, a/evaluate and w/audit,
                 because that scattering is correct layering, not a gap."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-07-spec-evaluation.md, Part V"}

    {:id        :standard-library-freeze
     :date      "2026-07-01"
     :decision  "No further grimoires are under active consideration for the
                 standard library. The scry candidate waits until this freeze is
                 explicitly revisited."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "conjurer.md, The grimoire ecosystem;
                 proposals/2026-07-spec-evaluation.md, Part V"}

    {:id        :no-hardcoded-counts
     :date      "2026-07-01"
     :decision  "Entry documents do not hardcode the symbol count; index.edn is
                 the one place it can be read. A hardcoded count had drifted."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md 1.2.0"}

    {:id        :notes-genre-contract
     :date      "2026-07-04"
     :decision  "Implementation notes for LLM processors follow one contract: a
                 modality scale (must and never bind; prefer and should yield
                 and are surfaced; flag means surface and continue), explicit
                 parameters over notes over examples, and layer attribution for
                 runtime properties."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md 1.2.0; template.md"}

    {:id        :intent-sourced-programming
     :date      "2026-07-08"
     :decision  "The paradigm is named intent-sourced programming: intent is the
                 source, code is the build. Distinguished from Spec-Driven
                 Development, where the specification is consumed once."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md 1.2.0; conjurer.md, What Conjurer is"}

    ;; ── Recovered: the October passes ───────────────────────────────

    {:id        :symmetric-form-shape
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "Every form has the shape (head name :param value ...), with
                 parameters in pairs. The phantom (context establish ...) broke
                 that symmetry and was removed everywhere."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md, Unreleased; template.md, Form shape"}

    {:id        :british-prose-stable-symbols
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "Prose uses British spelling. Symbol names and parameter
                 keywords keep their spelling (e/formalize, w/analyze): renaming
                 a symbol breaks every caller for a spelling preference."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "CHANGELOG.md, Unreleased; proposals/2026-10-spec-evaluation.md,
                 Part IV"}

    {:id        :three-version-lines
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "Three version lines run independently, each with one owner: the
                 specification release (package version, set by release-please
                 and followed by CHANGELOG.md), the catalogue in index.edn, and
                 each grimoire's own version. All follow semantic versioning."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-10-spec-evaluation.md, Part V (f/hoist
                 :version-model); template.md, Versioning"}

    {:id        :template-owns-cnj-structure
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "template.md Part II is the only place the .cnj structure is
                 defined: nine sections, abstractions and foresight included.
                 core.md and quick-reference.md point to it. Three copies had
                 already drifted once."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-10-spec-evaluation.md, Part V (f/hoist
                 :cnj-structure-owner)"}

    {:id        :decision-identifiers
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "Charter decisions carry :id when referred to and :supersedes
                 when reversing another; the log is append-only and a reversal is
                 a new entry."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-10-spec-evaluation.md, Part V (f/hoist
                 :decision-ids)"}

    {:id        :expression-prelude
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "A closed prelude lists the expressions a deterministic processor
                 may evaluate; every other head is a semantic function. The
                 determinism boundary became a property of the language rather
                 than a project rule."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-10-spec-evaluation.md, Part V (f/hoist
                 :expression-prelude)"}

    {:id        :confidence-two-axes
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "One confidence vocabulary on two axes, provenance and degree; a
                 number only with its basis named."
     :recovered :attested
     :source    "proposals/2026-10-spec-evaluation.md, Part V (f/hoist
                 :confidence-vocabulary)"}

    ;; ── Recovered from the maintainer's design notes ────────────────

    {:id        :house-rules
     :date      "2026-10-13"
     :decision  "Recorded as house rules, in force before this charter existed:
                 all canonical specification and design text is in English
                 whatever language the conversation is in, Dutch only where
                 localisation is itself the subject; Mermaid diagrams contain no
                 HTML markup and no emoji; form annotations document only
                 non-obvious external connections, never restate the code; an
                 asset's :conventions are plain prose rather than path
                 templates; elegance and simplicity are the primary design
                 criteria."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "the maintainer's design notes, kept from design conversations"
     :note      "The date is when they were recorded here, not when they were
                 decided; those dates and most of the reasons were not kept.
                 Each rule now has a dated entry with its reason; see
                 :decision/sessions-recovered and the entries after it."}

    ;; ── Authored 2026-10-13: Intent over vibes ──────────────────────

    {:id       :self-charter
     :date     "2026-10-13"
     :decision "Conjurer keeps its own charter, in design/conjurer.cnj. Its
                history is recovered from the CHANGELOG, the proposals, git and
                the design notes, each entry graded. Reason: the language says
                intent is the source and a decision log prevents re-arguing
                settled questions; it should hold its own reasons the same way.
                Two hoists of 2026-10-12 pointed at :decision/three-version-lines
                and :decision/template-owns-cnj-structure, which existed nowhere
                until now."}

    {:id       :transcripts-as-evidence
     :date     "2026-10-13"
     :decision "x/reconstruct-decisions reads session transcripts (:from
                :transcripts, located by :transcripts). A transcript is the one
                trace written while a decision was being made; it is read by
                speaker, so a model's untaken proposal is never recorded as the
                practitioner's decision, and output accepted without comment
                gets a :speculative why. exhume 2.0.0 -> 2.1.0, index.edn 2.0.0 ->
                2.1.0."}

    {:id       :variance-surface
     :date     "2026-10-13"
     :decision "core names the variance surface: the binding statements of a
                specification that only the :llm layer will honour. It is read
                off the form, listed by explain :show [:variance-surface], and
                reduced where it matters by writing a predicate in the prelude
                or naming :tests or :lint. Specification side only in this round;
                tool support is :variance-surface-report below. core 3.0.0 ->
                3.1.0."}

    {:id       :crystallisation
     :date     "2026-10-13"
     :decision "Conjurer does not forbid exploring by conversation; it absorbs
                it. conjurer.md says so under What Conjurer is not, and exhume
                gains the integration pattern Crystallising an exploratory
                prototype: explore, exhume the model and decisions, charter what
                survived, materialise from a preflight, park the rest in
                foresight, and explore again when a genuine unknown appears.
                Reason: specifying before discovery freezes ignorance, and
                discovering without crystallising loses what was found."}

    ;; ── Recovered 2026-10-13 from the design sessions ───────────────
    ;; The conversations in which the language was shaped, read by speaker
    ;; as :decision/transcripts-as-evidence prescribes. A choice the
    ;; maintainer stated or explicitly accepted is a decision. A reason in
    ;; his own words is given as his; a reason the model proposed and he
    ;; accepted is marked as the model's in :note; where he gave none, the
    ;; question stands in :open. Each date is the day the session was last
    ;; active. Proposals nobody took up appear only where they left a trace.

    {:id        :name-conjurer
     :date      "2025-10-31"
     :decision  "The language is called Conjurer. The maintainer's brief named
                 the reasons: the echo of Clojure and its conj, the automagical
                 feel of a language whose forms are manifested rather than
                 executed, and macros."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2025-10-31, Conjurer pseudo-programming language
                 design: the maintainer's opening turn"}

    {:id        :english-canonical
     :date      "2025-11-03"
     :decision  "English is the norm for keywords, model names and descriptions
                 in the specification; Dutch appears only to demonstrate a
                 :locale feature. Restated on 2026-06-01 and 2026-06-06, when
                 drafts in Dutch were sent back as not being English
                 instructions. Dates the first rule of :decision/house-rules."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2025-11-03, Semantics grimoire: the maintainer asked
                 for every Dutch keyword and model name to be translated;
                 sessions 2026-06-01 and 2026-06-06"
     :note      "The rule is stated as a norm here; the reasons followed on
                 2026-10-13 (:decision/english-why)."}

    {:id        :primitives-in-core
     :date      "2025-11-03"
     :decision  "The execution primitives (sequence, parallel, branch, retry,
                 intercept) went into core before orchestrate was written, and
                 orchestrate composes them: core holds the building blocks,
                 orchestrate the workflow patterns built from them."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2025-11-03, Essential grimoires for the library"
     :note      "The reason is the model's, accepted by the maintainer: without
                 the primitives in core, orchestrate would either absorb
                 low-level forms that belong in core or force core to be
                 retrofitted."}

    {:id        :nomenclature
     :date      "2025-11-07"
     :decision  "The core vocabulary is conjure, invocation, ritual, grimoire,
                 spell for a named definition, charm for an anonymous one and
                 incantation for a macro; grimoire is a declaration like
                 Clojure's ns, not a wrapper around its contents. The
                 maintainer's brief: themed terms from the start, mnemonic and
                 elegant, and not too many of them. His first ideas, spellbind
                 for a named definition and spell for an anonymous one, became
                 spell and charm. The forms entered core with
                 :decision/abstraction-layer."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2025-11-07, Conjurer terminology proposal"
     :note      "Why spell rather than spellbind is the model's argument
                 (shorter, composes better), accepted by the maintainer; the
                 grimoire-as-ns refinement is his."}

    {:id        :symbol-catalogue
     :date      "2025-11-07"
     :decision  "Every symbol belongs in one catalogue, so that a definition can
                 be told from an example and symbols and their dependencies can
                 be checked mechanically. The same proposal's scribe grimoire,
                 sigil metadata and ;;; form-declaration markers were never
                 adopted."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2025-11-07, Conjurer terminology proposal; the
                 repository holds index.edn and none of the rest"
     :note      "The aim is taken from the session's summary, not a verbatim
                 turn. That index.edn, introduced with the skill packaging on
                 2026-05-31, descends from this proposal is inferred from the
                 purpose they share."}

    {:id        :design-directory
     :date      "2026-05-31"
     :decision  ".cnj files live in design/ and are named by concern, never by
                 sequence: no numeric prefixes. design/ was the maintainer's own
                 first choice. On 2026-06-01 he restated the prefix rule as long
                 settled, for grimoire names too
                 (:decision/clean-grimoire-names)."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-05-31, Elevating Conjurer's core abstractions;
                 session 2026-06-01, Deterministic and probabilistic principles"
     :note      "The reasons against the alternatives are the model's, accepted:
                 dev/ suggests scripts, a hidden directory hides first-class
                 documents, specs/ sounds static. The maintainer's reason for the
                 prefix rule followed on 2026-10-13
                 (:decision/no-numeric-prefixes-why)."}

    {:id        :examples-generic
     :date      "2026-05-31"
     :decision  "Worked examples use generic business domains and name no
                 particular standard: the municipal enforcement roster in core
                 became a SaaS subscription platform, TSF++ became a team
                 coding standard, and wordguard was dropped as an example
                 because, as the maintainer put it, nobody knows it and it is a
                 side project."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-05-31, Elevating Conjurer's core abstractions:
                 the maintainer's turns"
     :note      "For the domain and the standard he asked for something more
                 generic without giving a further reason."}

    {:id        :handover-in-core
     :date      "2026-05-31"
     :decision  "handover belongs to core's ecosystem layer with charter, target
                 and asset, not to orchestrate. orchestrate coordinates what
                 happens inside a running system; handover moves context between
                 agents, sessions and tools, at the level of the project."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-05-31, Elevating Conjurer's core abstractions"
     :note      "The maintainer questioned the placement; the reason is the
                 model's answer, which he accepted."}

    {:id        :annotations-only-external
     :date      "2026-05-31"
     :decision  "Section dividers above forms were dropped, because a form
                 already states its kind and its name. A comment earns its place
                 only for a connection outside the file that the form cannot
                 state. Dates and gives the reason for the annotation rule in
                 :decision/house-rules."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-05-31: the maintainer asked why the divider was
                 needed, and accepted the answer"}

    {:id        :conventions-as-prose
     :date      "2026-05-31"
     :decision  "An asset's :conventions are plain-language principles, not path
                 templates. A template duplicates the layout, diverges when the
                 code is reorganised and claims a precision that holds for one
                 layout only; a principle lets the model derive a place and say
                 that it did. A structured :structure field may follow once real
                 projects show which conventions are stable. Dates and gives the
                 reason for the :conventions rule in :decision/house-rules."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-05-31, Elevating Conjurer's core abstractions"
     :note      "The reason is the model's; the maintainer accepted it with the
                 rest of that round."}

    {:id        :plan-before-write
     :date      "2026-05-31"
     :decision  "Materialisation plans before it writes, a dry run ships before
                 write mode, and rewriting existing files to changed conventions
                 is a separate operation from materialising new ones, because
                 the two carry different risks. The forerunner of
                 :decision/materialise-two-phase."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-05-31: review of an IDE agent's analysis of
                 materialisation"
     :note      "The reasoning is the model's, accepted by the maintainer."}

    {:id        :branding
     :date      "2026-05-31"
     :decision  "The README shows Hieronymus Bosch's The Conjurer, the
                 maintainer's choice, under an epigraph from Marlowe's Doctor
                 Faustus. The epigraph follows a Clojure custom he cited: a
                 literary citation at the head of a project, as Leiningen has."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-05-31: the maintainer's turn on the README"
     :note      "The lines from Faustus are the model's suggestion, adopted
                 without comment: their three wishes read as conjure, explain and
                 a/delegate."}

    {:id        :elegance-first
     :date      "2026-06-01"
     :decision  "Elegance and simplicity are the maintainer's starting point for
                 almost every choice, as he put it when choosing the certainty
                 qualifiers. Dates the last rule of :decision/house-rules; the
                 rule is his own design value rather than a derived one."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-06-01, Deterministic and probabilistic principles"}

    {:id        :calibrated-certainty
     :date      "2026-06-01"
     :decision  "Certainty is expressed at two grains: the inline qualifiers
                 certain, prefer and allow on values, and the contract pair
                 given and ensure around an invocation, with a philosophy
                 section in conjurer.md. The maintainer chose the qualifiers as
                 the most elegant option and kept given and ensure beside them,
                 because the qualifiers grade freedom but do not separate before
                 from after."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-06-01, Deterministic and probabilistic principles:
                 the maintainer's turns"
     :note      "The model asked whether prefer clashes with :prefers; the
                 question went unanswered and the name stayed. core argues that
                 the two work at different levels, value and capability."}

    {:id        :context-establish-dropped
     :date      "2026-06-01"
     :decision  "(context establish name ...) was removed from core. The
                 maintainer's reasons: it put a verb between head and name,
                 breaking the pattern of every other form, and conjurer-mcp had
                 tripped over it. The copies left in other files went on
                 2026-10-12 (:decision/symmetric-form-shape)."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-06-01, Deterministic and probabilistic principles"}

    {:id        :greenfield-cleanup
     :date      "2026-06-01"
     :decision  "No backward compatibility while the language was greenfield:
                 references to earlier versions were removed from core and the
                 grimoire-level :version was dropped. The maintainer's reason:
                 demo code that depended on the specification could be patched,
                 and conjurer-mcp might be overhauled."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-06-01, Deterministic and probabilistic principles"
     :note      "Dropping :version was the model's reading of that brief. Since
                 reversed in part: :decision/three-version-lines gives each
                 grimoire its version back, and
                 :decision/british-prose-stable-symbols keeps symbol names
                 stable for the sake of callers."}

    {:id        :mermaid-plain-text
     :date      "2026-06-01"
     :decision  "Mermaid diagrams use plain-text labels, because HTML markup
                 showed up literally in the renderer; emoji are not used at all.
                 Dates the Mermaid rule of :decision/house-rules and gives the
                 reason for its HTML half."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-06-01: the maintainer's turn on the diagrams"
     :note      "The reason for the emoji ban followed on 2026-10-13
                 (:decision/no-emoji-why)."}

    {:id        :determinism-boundary-reasons
     :date      "2026-06-06"
     :decision  "The maintainer's own reasons for :decision/determinism-boundary:
                 a server without a model can still hold workspace knowledge,
                 parse, resolve and remember, and so save tokens and room in the
                 context window; the work that needs judgement, exhume and
                 materialise above all, stays with the model in the editor."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-06-06, conjurer-mcp without an embedded model: the
                 maintainer's opening turn"}

    {:id        :exhume-origin
     :date      "2026-06-09"
     :decision  "exhume answered a concrete need: recover the earlier conjurer-mcp
                 codebase into .cnj files, then rebuild the server from the
                 updated specification. x/recover-stack followed when the first
                 real exhume run showed dependencies and lint configuration only
                 as incidental evidence. Gives the origin of
                 :decision/exhume-as-inverse."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-06-09, Improvement iterations: the maintainer's
                 four-step plan, and the IDE agent's exhume run"}

    {:id        :delegated-adoption
     :date      "2026-10-12"
     :decision  "The maintainer delegated the adoption of the October
                 evaluation's recommended candidates: he trusted the analysis and
                 said to go ahead in full. The reasons recorded for
                 :decision/three-version-lines,
                 :decision/template-owns-cnj-structure,
                 :decision/decision-identifiers, :decision/expression-prelude and
                 :decision/confidence-two-axes are therefore the evaluation's,
                 adopted on that delegation and confirmed by his merge."
     :recovered :strongly-inferred
     :source    "session 2026-10-12, Conjurer core improvements"}

    {:id       :sessions-recovered
     :date     "2026-10-13"
     :decision "The design sessions of 2025-10-31 to 2026-10-12 were read by
                speaker (:decision/transcripts-as-evidence) and the decisions
                they hold appended to this log, graded and sourced, with the
                maintainer's reasons kept apart from the model's. The log is the
                record; the transcripts are not copied into it."}

    {:id       :english-why
     :date     "2026-10-13"
     :decision "The maintainer's reasons for :decision/english-canonical:
                computer science largely works in English, and many of the
                terms Conjurer uses are best captured in it; English reaches a
                far larger potential audience; and a Dutch specification would
                still have to borrow English terms, or look up or invent Dutch
                ones."}

    {:id       :no-emoji-why
     :date     "2026-10-13"
     :decision "The maintainer's reason for the emoji half of
                :decision/mermaid-plain-text: emoji almost always look cheap."}

    {:id       :no-numeric-prefixes-why
     :date     "2026-10-13"
     :decision "The maintainer's reason for :decision/clean-grimoire-names and
                :decision/design-directory: numeric prefixes on file names are
                not idiomatic in programming languages, and he does not like
                them. The model's earlier reason, that order comes from the
                dependency graph, agrees with this but is not his."}]

  :open [
    "Should this file be validated by conjurer-mcp in CI, and in which
     validate_cnj mode: authored, or recovered for its history?"
    "Do the live candidates graded in proposals/ (:scry-grimoire,
     :primitive-time-by-parameter, :names-are-symbols) move into Section 8
     of this file, or stay in the evaluation that graded them?"]

  :references ["../examples/conjurer-mcp/conjurer-mcp.cnj"]
  :tags       [:language :specification :meta])

;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;; Section 2 — Assets
;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(asset :grimoire-template
  :type        :code-standard
  :description "The structure every grimoire follows, the form-shape and
                versioning rules, the implementation-notes contract, and the
                one definition of the .cnj file structure."
  :language    :markdown
  :location    "../template.md"
  :enforces    [:canonical-grimoire-structure :form-shape :three-version-lines
                :implementation-notes-contract]
  :applies-to  [:grimoire :cnj-file :entry-document]
  :active-in   :project)

(asset :symbol-catalogue
  :type        :api-specification
  :description "Every symbol across the grimoires with its key parameters, and
                the prelude a deterministic processor may evaluate. The routing
                layer for processors and tools."
  :language    :edn
  :location    "../index.edn"
  :applies-to  [:grimoire :entry-document :tooling]
  :active-in   :project)

;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;; Section 3 — Assumptions
;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(assume
  :environment    :specification-repository
  :team           {:size 1 :skill-level :expert}
  :infrastructure {:existing [:github :release-please :conjurer-mcp]
                   :avoid    [:model-embedded-in-tooling]}
  :non-negotiable [:english-canonical-text :append-only-decisions
                   :graded-recovery :no-fabricated-rationale]
  :negotiable     [:grimoire-count :entry-document-layout])

;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;; Section 8 — Foresight
;;; ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

(f/candidate :variance-surface-report
  :label     "conjurer-mcp reports the variance surface of a .cnj file"
  :added     "2026-10-13"
  :status    :proposed
  :scores    {:feasibility 7 :elegance 8 :containment 8 :value 8}
  :rationale "The classification is mechanical — prelude membership,
              :verify-via, and which structural checkers the server offers — so
              a deterministic processor can produce it without generating
              anything. A tool would let a practitioner see, before
              materialising, which binding statements nothing will check.
              Deferred because the specification side had to land first."
  :conditions ["the prelude evaluator is merged in conjurer-mcp"
               "the server can enumerate the structural checkers it offers"]
  :cluster   :variance)

(f/candidate :intent-health-check
  :label     "A lint for specification debt in .cnj files"
  :added     "2026-10-13"
  :status    :proposed
  :scores    {:feasibility 6 :elegance 7 :containment 8 :value 8}
  :rationale "Flags decisions without a reason, :requires entries no target or
              ensure covers, and candidates never reassessed. Catches the spec
              theatre the variance surface does not: intent that is written but
              holds nothing. Builds on the health module in conjurer-mcp."
  :conditions ["check_references is in place, so coverage can be traced"
               "the thresholds (how old is a stale candidate) are decided by
                the maintainer, not inferred"]
  :cluster   :variance)

(f/candidate :divergence-probe
  :label     "Materialise one charter twice and read the differences as
              underspecified intent"
  :added     "2026-10-13"
  :status    :proposed
  :scores    {:feasibility 5 :elegance 9 :containment 7 :value 8}
  :rationale "Turns the model's variance from a risk into a detector: where two
              faithful manifestations of the same specification differ, the
              specification did not decide. Broken symmetry informs. Low
              feasibility because the generation runs on the IDE side, outside
              the deterministic tooling."
  :conditions ["two manifestations can be compared structurally, not only as
                text"]
  :cluster   :variance)

(f/candidate :sketch-mode
  :label     "An explicit exploratory mode in the language (recommendation:
              abandon)"
  :added     "2026-10-13"
  :status    :proposed
  :scores    {:feasibility 6 :elegance 4 :containment 4 :value 5}
  :rationale "The obvious way to bring exploration into the language. But allow
              and progressive refinement already leave room to explore, and a
              mode that relaxes the topology would blur exactly the distinctions
              intent topology exists to keep. Exploration belongs outside the
              charter; crystallisation (:decision/crystallisation) brings its
              results in. Recorded so the reasoning stays visible; the low
              elegance score is the finding."
  :conditions ["practitioners are observed abusing allow to mean 'not yet
                decided' at scale"]
  :cluster   :exploration)
